r membership created A system or mechanism used to identify a user through for a person, group, or machine entity that grant access to associating an incoming request with a set of identifying resources or functionalities within a computer system or credentials. The credentials provided are compared to network. A system of accounts is important for managing those on a file in a database of the authorized user’s permissions and security levels across an enterprise, information on a local operating system, user directory and an individual may have access to multiple accounts service, or within an authentication server. Examples of depending on job roles and security requirements. User authentication systems can include active directory, Multi- accounts are for individual users and are tailored for the Factor Authentication (MFA), biometrics, and tokens. specific tasks their roles and responsibilities require. User accounts, administrator accounts, and service accounts Authorization systems are subsets of accounts. A system or mechanism used to determine access levels or user/client privileges related to system resources including Administrator accounts files, services, computer programs, data, and application Accounts for users requiring escalated privileges. The features. An authorization system grants or denies access accounts are used for managing aspects of a computer, to a resource based on the user’s identity. Examples of domain, or the whole enterprise information technology authorization systems can include active directory, access infrastructure. Each administrator account should be control lists, and role-based access control lists. assigned to a single user. Common administrator account subtypes include root accounts, local administrator, Bi-annually domain administrator accounts, and network or security Every six months. Any tasks that should be done bi- appliance administrator accounts. annually should also be repeated whenever significant change has occurred that would affect the network or Application Programming Interface (API) devices in question, including changes such as hardware A set of rules and interfaces for software components to upgrades or mergers and acquisitions. interact with each other in a standardized way. APIs allow applications to access and communicate with both internal Breach and external resources.1 The loss of control, compromise, unauthorized disclosure, unauthorized acquisition, or any similar occurrence where: Applications a person other than an authorized user accesses or A program, or a group of programs, running on top of an potentially accesses sensitive or confidential information; operating system hosted on an enterprise asset. Example or an authorized user accesses sensitive or confidential application types include web, database, cloud-based, and information for other than authorized purposes. mobile. Applications are considered a software asset in this document. Cloud environment A virtualized environment that provides convenient, on- Asset Class demand network access to a shared pool of configurable A group of information assets that are evaluated as one set resources such as network, computing, storage, based on their similarity. Devices, Software, Data, Users, applications, and services. There are five essential Network, and Documentation are examples. characteristics to a cloud environment: on-demand self- service, broad network access, resource pooling, rapid elasticity, and measured service. Some services offered through cloud environments include Software as a Service (SaaS), Platform as a Service (PaaS), and Infrastructure as a Service (IaaS). 1 NIST: https://csrc.nist.gov/glossary/term/application_programming_interface A4 Glossary CIS Controls v8.1.2 Data Enterprise assets A collection of facts that can be examined, considered, and Assets with the potential to store or process data. For the used for decision-making. Although data may be physical, purpose of this docume