program. media include CDs, DVDs, Blu‑ray Discs, external hard drives, SD cards, tape backups, diskettes, and USB drives. Portable devices Transportable, end-user devices that have the capability Script to wirelessly connect to a network. Portable devices can Uncompiled code that requires a software include laptops which may require external hardware for environment to execute. connectivity and mobile devices, such as smartphones and tablets. For the purpose of this document, portable devices are a subset of end-user devices. Sensitive Data Physical or digital data stored, processed, or managed by Pretexting the enterprise that must be kept private, accurate, reliable, and available. If released or destroyed in an unauthorized Part of a social engineering attack that involves inventing manner, it would cause harm to the enterprise or its a scenario to convince the victim to divulge information customers. These impacts may be due to a data breach or that should not be divulged. The purpose of pretexting is to a violation of a policy, contract, or regulation. convince the victim of the legitimacy of the communication. The method of this type of attack can be through any communication method or medium. 4 https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4949 Servers Software A device or system that provides resources, data, services, Sets of data and instructions used to direct a computer to or programs to other devices on either a local area network complete a specific task. Software assets include operating or wide area network. Servers can provide resources systems and applications. Both may contain services, and use them from another system at the same time. libraries, or Application Programming Interfaces (APIs). Servers can exist in datacenters, public/private/hybrid cloud environments, including temporal containers or Tailgating serverless workloads. Examples of servers include web servers, application servers, mail servers, and file servers. A physical security issue where an individual For the purpose of this document, servers are a subset of follows another into a secured area without properly enterprise assets. authenticating or following established protocols for entering the area. Service accounts A service account is created specifically to run Third-Party Provider applications, services, and automated tasks on an See Service Provider. operating system. Service accounts may also be created just to own data and configuration files. Each service Users account should be used for a specific service or function, Employees, third-party vendors, contractors, service and it should have an assigned owner who is responsible providers, consultants, or any other person who is for how the account is used. Service accounts should not authorized to access an enterprise asset. This also includes be used for general purpose computing. user, administrator, and service accounts. Services User accounts Specialized programs that perform well-defined critical An identity comprised of a set of credentials (e.g., tasks for the operating system. Services often start with username, password) that defines a user on a computer the operating system, run-in in the background, and or computing system. A user account keeps track of a can be stopped and started by users. Example services user’s information and settings, controls the files, folders, include managing network communications, users, file and resources a user is allowed to access, as well as the permissions, system security, and device interaction. tasks a user is allowed to perform. For the purpose of this document, user accounts refer to “standard” user accounts Service Provider with limited privileges and are used for general tasks. Entity that offers platforms, software, and services to other enterprises. Examples include IT consultants, Virtual environment managed service provider (MSPs), Software as a Service Simulates hardware to allow a software environment (SaaS) platforms, and cloud service prov